From 401d2175b531c9aa3864c2954130477de847538a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:37:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] API 33: bow-like mod items (behaves_as), item-released,
 item-shot and entities.set-entity-fire

A content mod's item records the vanilla item it copies (horizon:behaves_as), and the game's checks by item id for the bow (use, release, FOV, trigger feel, hands) read it through Items::behaves_as, so a mod item with template minecraft:bow draws and shoots as a bow. registration.item-release turns on item-released (false cancels the shot) and item-shot (the arrows' entity ids exist). set-entity-fire lights a mob or an arrow in flight.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RYe92n7spgy8vtm4CovRWA
